※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4616 LANG_ARENA_NOT_YOURS_TO_EMPTY

※ Only what made an arena gives it back.  One handed over by reference is its maker's, who
※ may be holding things made in it; `⎕heap` and an arena at the top level last as long as
※ the program, and anything may be holding things made in those.

fn cleared(a: &mut arena) → u8:
    ⎕empty(a)
    0u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let scratch: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(scratch)
    if cleared(&mut scratch) = 0u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
